## Testing Patterns

### ✅ Component Testing
```javascript
// ✅ Simple component tests
describe('ParticipantCard', () => {
  it('displays participant information', () => {
    const participant = { name: 'John Doe', region: 'Berlin' };
    render(<ParticipantCard participant={participant} />);
    
    expect(screen.getByText('John Doe')).toBeInTheDocument();
    expect(screen.getByText('Berlin')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```

### ✅ Hook Testing
```javascript
// ✅ Custom hook tests
describe('useParticipants', () => {
  it('fetches participants successfully', async () => {
    const mockParticipants = [{ id: 1, name: 'John Doe' }];
    global.fetch = jest.fn().mockResolvedValue({
      json: () => Promise.resolve({ success: true, data: mockParticipants })
    });

    const { result } = renderHook(() => useParticipants());
    
    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(result.current.data).toEqual(mockParticipants);
    });
  });
});
```

## API Route Patterns

### ✅ Express Route Structure
```javascript
// ✅ Simple route handlers
router.get('/participants', async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const participants = await executeQuery('SELECT * FROM participants');
    res.json({ success: true, data: participants });
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });
  }
});
```

### ✅ Admin Routes
```javascript
// ✅ Admin routes with middleware
router.post('/participants', ...adminMiddleware(), async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const { name, region, instagram } = req.body;
    const result = await executeQuery(
      'INSERT INTO participants (name, region, instagram) VALUES ($1, $2, $3) RETURNING *',
      [name, region, instagram]
    );
    res.json({ success: true, data: result.rows[0] });
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });
  }
});
```

## Development Commands

### ✅ Essential Commands
```bash
# Development
npm run dev              # Start both frontend and backend
npm run dev:client       # Frontend only (port 5173)
npm run dev:server       # Backend only (port 3005)

# Testing
npm test                 # Run all tests
npm run test:watch      # Watch mode
npm run test:coverage    # Coverage report

# Database
npm run migrate         # Run database migrations
npm run seed            # Seed test data

# Production
npm run build           # Build for production
npm start               # Start production server
```

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### ❌ Complex State Management
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T use complex stores
const store = useComplexStore();
const websocket = useWebSocket();
```

### ❌ Over-Engineering
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom abstractions
class CustomDatabaseWrapper {}
const customAuthService = new CustomAuthService();
```

### ❌ WebSocket Infrastructure
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T use WebSockets
const socket = io('ws://localhost:3000');
socket.on('update', handleUpdate);
```

